  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Tyler Mahle couldn't hold the early lead. Arizona scored six runs after the second inning and the Giants left one runner in scoring position in the fifth, the only real chance they created down two.",
    "what_this_means": "This is what slipping looks like from the inside. They held a lead in the second inning, then watched it evaporate across two innings of damage. Three runs in the third, three more in the fifth. The offense managed eight hits but converted one of five runners in scoring position into a run. That's not inconsistency showing up again. That's inconsistency becoming a grid. Keaton Winn threw three shutout strikeouts out of the bullpen, but that precision couldn't carry a game the bats didn't finish. They need one more swing from one more player in one more late inning. They haven't found it yet.",
    "what_to_watch": "Davis Martin's ERA sits at 1.61 for Chicago. Tomorrow night at 7:15 PT, Trevor McDonald takes the mound fresh off a 2.46 ERA over his last three starts. A clear advantage against a Sox lineup that has been quiet early in the season.",
